  body: "# Recoverability of overpaid benefit in DMG chapter 9\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe chapter distinguishes
    an overpayment from the decision that an amount is recoverable, including the relevant benefit, grounds, person,
    period and supporting entitlement decision.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is the chapter 9 route, not a
    universal recoverability rule for all benefits. Misrepresentation and non-disclosure are distinguished; DMG
    09168 describes other recovery contexts. Do not apply this summary to Universal Credit or infer fraud.\n\n##
    Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 09024, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09029, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09164, PDF page 36](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=36)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09168, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=37)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch9` PDF SHA-256: `96933fc64fcacb0a3e253a686218757a85fb415574fde11e4d3435149b1a2505`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `069cefdb6e8a7486021d251c6991ef627fc063a3b842eff2e98cde688ed831d2`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
